From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: denchiklut <ollylut@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 09:15:38 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] oa: recycle a page view's compositor, as ArcCore does

Restores ui::RecyclableCompositorMacFactory, which upstream removed: a BrowserCompositorMac that leaves HasOwnCompositor gives its RecyclableCompositorMac to a pool of at most one spare, and the next one that enters it takes that spare instead of building a new compositor. Only a page's view (WebContentsViewMac::CreateViewForWidget) recycles; a popup's compositor is marked non-recyclable and deleted, as in ArcCore, whose RenderWidgetHostViewMac and BrowserCompositorMac take the same added flag. An embedder that hosts the page's NSView itself, outside views' parent ui::Layer, otherwise shows nothing on every tab switch until the new compositor's first frame. BrowserCompositorMac::DisableRecyclingForShutdown() empties the pool before the context factory goes.

Viz sends a root compositor's CALayerParams again only when they change, and a recycled compositor's don't, so as in ArcCore ui::AcceleratedWidgetMac keeps its last params when its view is reset (recording new ones while suspended in the pool) and hands them to the next view it is set on. The pool resets a compositor's background to transparent and suspends its widget, as ArcCore's does; Oa also keeps its compositor lock on a pooled compositor, which ArcCore doesn't, because an unlocked one draws an empty frame that the next view shows. As ArcCore: a view that takes fallback content from another (a navigation's new widget) builds its next compositor anew, the other's compositor isn't pooled, and RenderWidgetHostViewMac::TakeFallbackContentFrom shows the view's own last frame again when it already has one.
